The '''2025–26 Thai League 1''' was the 9th season of [[Thai League 1]] under its current name and the 29th season of top-flight Thai [[Association football|football]] professional league since its establishment in 1996. This league is also known as '''BYD Sealion 6 League I''' due to the sponsorship deal with [[BYD Auto]]. The season began on 15 August 2025 and concluded on 10 May 2026. 

[[Buriram United F.C.|Buriram United]] entered the season as the [[List of Thai football champions|four-time defending champions]], having won their fourth consecutive league title and 11th overall Thai top-flight football title the previous season.<ref>{{cite web |title=Buriram blitz seals 10th title |work=Bangkok Post |url=https://www.bangkokpost.com/sports/3015791/buriram-blitz-seals-10th-title |last1=Chittinand |first1=Tor |date=2 May 2025 }}</ref>

== Overview ==
=== Promotion and relegation (pre-season) ===
16 teams will compete in the league – the thirteen teams from previous season and three teams promoted from [[2024–25 Thai League 2|Thai League 2]].

==== Teams promoted from Thai League 2 ====
[[Chonburi F.C.|Chonburi]] and [[Ayutthaya United F.C.|Ayutthaya United]] became the first two teams to be promoted on 26 April 2025 after winning their respective matches. Chonburi were also crowned champions by defeating [[Suphanburi F.C.|Suphanburi]] 0–1 in an away match, while Ayutthaya United beat [[Bangkok F.C.|Bangkok]] 5–1. [[Kanchanaburi Power F.C.|Kanchanaburi Power]] became the last team to be promoted after their win against [[Phrae United F.C.|Phrae United]] 4–5 on aggregate in promotion play-off match.

Chonburi returned to the top division after a one-season absence, while for Ayutthaya United and Kanchanaburi Power this was their first season in the top division in their history, respectively.<ref>{{Cite AV media |url=https://shows.acast.com/chiang-mai-is-blue/episodes/chonburi-take-the-t2-title |title=Chonburi take the T2 title {{!}} The original Chiang Mai is Blue |date=2025-04-30 |access-date=2025-06-12 |via=shows.acast.com}}</ref>

==== Teams relegated to Thai League 2 ====
[[Khon Kaen United F.C.|Khonkaen United]] became the first team to be relegated on 30 March 2025 after suffering a 0–5 defeat to [[Bangkok United F.C.|Bangkok United]]. The result ended their time in the top division for 4 seasons.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=1 April 2025 |title=Khon Kaen relegated to second tier after heavy defeat |url=https://bangkokpost.com/sports/2992116/khon-kaen-relegated-to-second-tier-after-heavy-defeat/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250402224754/https://bangkokpost.com/sports/2992116/khon-kaen-relegated-to-second-tier-after-heavy-defeat/ |archive-date=2025-04-02 |access-date=14 April 2025 |website=Bangkok Post |language=en}}</ref>

[[Nakhon Pathom United F.C.|Nakhon Pathom United]] became the second team to be relegated on 13 April 2025 after earning a 2–2 draw against [[Port F.C.|Port]]. The result ended their time in the top division for 2 seasons.<ref>{{Cite news |last=Chittinand |first=Tor |date=2025-04-14 |title=Port draw sends Nakhon Pathom down to tier two |url=https://www.bangkokpost.com/sports/3003087/port-draw-sends-nakhon-pathom-down-to-tier-two |access-date=2025-06-12 |work=Bangkok Post |language=en}}</ref>

[[Nongbua Pitchaya F.C.|Nongbua Pitchaya]] became the third and final team to be relegated after suffering a 1–2 defeat to Port and [[Rayong F.C.|Rayong]]'s win over Khonkaen United on 20 April 2025. These results meant that Nongbua Pitchaya only lasted one season in the top division and returned to the second division.<ref>{{Cite web |last= |first= |date=21 April 2025 |title=Rayong survive, Nongbua relegated in T1 drama |url=https://bangkokpost.com/sports/3008009/rayong-survive-nongbua-relegated-in-t1-drama/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20250422041456/https://bangkokpost.com/sports/3008009/rayong-survive-nongbua-relegated-in-t1-drama/ |archive-date=2025-04-22 |access-date=24 April 2025 |website=Bangkok Post |language=en}}</ref>

